{"slug": "jean-georges-vongerichtens-ginger-vinaigrette", "nyt_id": 1012698, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012698-jean-georges-vongerichtens-ginger-vinaigrette", "name": "Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s Ginger Vinaigrette", "author": "Mark Bittman", "description": "This recipe is an adaptation of one found in Jean-Georges Vongerichten’s and Mark Bittman's cookbook, “Jean-Georges: Cooking at Home with a Four-Star Chef.” Fresh ginger, lime juice and sherry vinegar are the star players in this simple, sophisticated dressing that will make any salad sing. After putting it together, let it rest for a day so the flavors can meld. Mark Bittman", "servings": {"text": "1 cups", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "volume"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 10, "raw": {"total": "PT10M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 cup extra virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "extra virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 2-inch piece of ginger, peeled and roughly chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": null, "item": "inch piece of ginger", "preparation": "peeled and roughly chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 tablespoon sherry vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sherry vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons fresh lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fresh lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "None"}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 193.3, "protein_g": null, "carbohydrates_g": 0.6, "fat_g": 21.6, "saturated_fat_g": 3.0, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.3, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 64.5, "fiber_g": 0.1, "sugar_g": 0.1, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["condiments"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "ginger", "quick"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/08/dining/08GINGERVINAGRETTE/08GINGERVINAGRETTE-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2015/06/08/dining/08GINGERVINAGRETTE/08GINGERVINAGRETTE-facebookJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 402}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-07-22", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:27:46Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jeffrey-steingartens-pizza-dough", "nyt_id": 1012488, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012488-jeffrey-steingartens-pizza-dough", "name": "Jeffrey Steingarten's Pizza Dough", "author": "Sam Sifton", "description": "Sam Sifton", "servings": {"text": "2 balls", "min": 2, "max": 2, "yield_type": "pieces"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 1650, "raw": {"total": "P1DT3H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "1 ½ cups unbleached all-purpose flour", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "unbleached all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ cups unbleached bread flour, plus more for dusting", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "unbleached bread flour", "preparation": "plus more for dusting", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "¾ teaspoon active dry yeast", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "tsp", "item": "active dry yeast", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 ¼ teaspoons Diamond Crystal kosher salt", "group": null, "quantity": 2.25, "unit": "tsp", "item": "diamond crystal kosher salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "3 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "The morning or ideally the day before cooking, prepare the dough. Using a hand whisk, combine the flours, yeast and salt in the bowl of an electric mixer. Switch to a wooden spoon and stir in 1 ½ cups cold water and olive oil until a rough dough forms. Set the bowl on the mixer and, using the paddle attachment, mix on low speed for 1 minute. Increase the speed to high and beat for 4 to 6 minutes, until it becomes a wet and vaguely menacing mass. (If it forms into a ball, lower the mixer speed to medium-high. If not, stop the mixer to scrape down the sides once.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "Scrape and pour the dough onto a heavily floured work surface. Keeping your fingers, the countertop and the dough well floured, fold one dough end over the other so that half the floured underside covers the rest of the dough. Let rest for 10 minutes."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Cut the dough into 2 equal pieces. Shape each piece into a smooth ball. Place each ball on a well-oiled plate, generously dust with flour and loosely cover with plastic wrap. Let the dough rise until it is at least doubled in size, about 3 hours."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Punch the dough balls down, shape into rounds and place each in a quart-size freezer bag. Refrigerate dough between 1 and 24 hours."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 896.0, "protein_g": 22.6, "carbohydrates_g": 146.6, "fat_g": 23.0, "saturated_fat_g": 3.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 3.3, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 507.5, "fiber_g": 5.4, "sugar_g": 0.6, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["main-course-pizza-and-calzones"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["active-dry-yeast", "all-purpose-flour", "bread-flour"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 109}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-04-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:21:44Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "jelly-doughnut-pudding", "nyt_id": 1012656, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012656-jelly-doughnut-pudding", "name": "Jelly Doughnut Pudding", "author": "Alex Witchel", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "8 to 10 servings", "min": 8, "max": 10, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 150, "raw": {"total": "PT2H30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 ½ cups heavy cream, at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 3.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": "at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ cups whole milk, at room temperature", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole milk", "preparation": "at room temperature", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ cups plus 2 tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus 2 tablespoons sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "8 large eggs", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": null, "item": "large eggs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "4 large egg yolks", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "large egg yolks", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "14 jelly doughnuts, preferably filled with raspberry jam", "group": null, "quantity": 14.0, "unit": null, "item": "jelly doughnuts", "preparation": "preferably filled with raspberry jam", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "Butter, for greasing pan", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "butter", "preparation": "for greasing pan", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Heat oven to 325 degrees. Fill a kettle with water and place over high heat to bring to a boil. In a large mixing bowl, combine cream, milk, 1 ½ cups sugar, eggs, egg yolks and vanilla. Whisk to blend."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Using a serrated knife, gently slice doughnuts from top to bottom in ¼-inch slices. Butter a 9-by-12-inch baking pan and sprinkle with 1 tablespoon sugar. Pour about ½ inch of the cream mixture into pan. Arrange a layer of sliced doughnuts in pan, overlapping them slightly. Top with another layer, pressing them down slightly to moisten them. Top with a small amount of cream mixture."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Arrange 2 more layers of sliced doughnuts, and pour remaining liquid evenly over top. Press down gently to moisten. Sprinkle with remaining 1 tablespoon sugar. Cover pan tightly with foil, and place in a larger pan. Fill larger pan with boiling water until three-quarters up the side of pudding pan."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Bake for 1 hour 50 minutes. Remove foil and continue to bake until top is golden brown, about 15 minutes. Turn off oven, open door slightly, and leave in oven for an additional 10 minutes. Serve warm or at room temperature."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 590.1, "protein_g": 9.7, "carbohydrates_g": 50.8, "fat_g": 39.3, "saturated_fat_g": 23.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 2.5, "trans_fat_g": 1.0, "cholesterol_mg": 326.5, "sodium_mg": 105.3, "fiber_g": 0.2, "sugar_g": 46.6, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["bread-pudding-dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": []}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 9}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-01-28"